email.org_deletion_cancelled.body:
Hi {name},

{actor} cancelled the deletion of {org}. Nothing was removed.

{url}

email.ownership_offer_sent.body:
Hi {name},

You asked {target} to become the owner of {org}. You stay the owner until they accept, and you can cancel here:

{url}

email.ownership_offer_declined.body:
Hi {name},

{target} declined to become the owner of {org}. You are still the owner.

{url}

email.ownership_received.body:
Hi {name},

You are now the owner of {org}, taking over from {other}. {other} stays an Org Admin.

{url}

email.ownership_handed_over.body:
Hi {name},

{other} accepted ownership of {org}. You are now an Org Admin there.

{url}

email.storage_disconnected.body:
Hi {name},

{actor} disconnected the storage bucket {bucket} from {org}. Files already in {bucket} stay there, but they can no longer be opened in {org}; connecting the same bucket again — same account or region, same name — brings them back; a bucket with the same name in another account does not. New uploads use {org}'s built-in storage again and count against its limit.

{url}

